ents or scoped form and\nfield groups instead of casting each field value."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"async-defaults-do-not-update","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Async defaults do not update"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Vue adapter observes reactive option objects. If data arrives after\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useForm"},{"type":"text","value":" runs, update "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" through a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reactive"},{"type":"text","value":" options object or\nmount the editor only after the data exists. A plain object containing a\none-time snapshot is not reactive."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"composition-types-fail-under-vue-3-5","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Composition types fail under Vue 3.5"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Form v2 requires Vue 3.6 or newer. The adapter's typed field components,\ninjection-based "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AppForm"},{"type":"text","value":", and form composition rely on Vue 3.6 behavior that\nis not available in Vue 3.5."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-instantiation-is-excessively-deep","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type instantiation is excessively deep"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This TypeScript error usually involves a very large recursive value shape, a\nwidely inferred union, or unsupported composition. Reduce it to the smallest\nform that reproduces the problem, keep "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" concrete, and avoid\nunnecessary generic wrappers."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the minimal reproduction still fails, report it in the\n"},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/form/issues","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Form issue tracker"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Include\nthe Vue and TypeScript versions, the form value type, and the smallest failing\nfield."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"errors-exist-but-are-not-displayed","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Errors exist but are not displayed"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.errors"},{"type":"text","value":" respects the form's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"errorVisibility"},{"type":"text","value":" policy. Inspect\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.meta.original.errors"},{"type":"text","value":" when debugging whether validation ran but the\nissues are intentionally hidden. Also confirm that the input calls\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.handleBlur"},{"type":"text","value":" if the policy depends on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isBlurred"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"an-input-initially-renders-undefined","text":"An input initially renders undefined","level":2},{"id":"a-field-value-is-unknown","text":"A field value is unknown","level":2},{"id":"async-defaults-do-not-update","text":"Async defaults do not update","level":2},{"id":"composition-types-fail-under-vue-3-5","text":"Composition types fail under Vue 3.5","level":2},{"id":"type-instantiation-is-excessively-deep","text":"Type instantiation is excessively deep","level":2},{"id":"errors-exist-but-are-not-displayed","text":"Errors exist but are not displayed","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThis page covers common Vue and TypeScript problems when using TanStack Form.\n\n## An input initially renders `undefined`\n\nEvery value rendered by an input must exist in form-level `defaultValues` from\nthe first render.\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { useForm } from '@tanstack/vue-form'\n\nconst form = useForm({\n  defaultValues: {\n    firstName: '',\n    subscribed: false,\n  },\n})\n</script>\n```\n\nDo not omit `defaultValues` or rely on a field-level default. When values come\nfrom an API, render a loading state before mounting the editable form or supply\na complete fallback shape.\n\n## A field value is `unknown`\n\nField names and values are inferred from `defaultValues`. Check that you have\nnot widened the initial object to `Record<string, unknown>`, `any`, or an\nunrelated union. Prefer a concrete value type:\n\n```ts\ntype Profile = { firstName: string; age: number }\n\nconst defaults: Profile = { firstName: '', age: 0 }\nconst form = useForm({ defaultValues: defaults })\n```\n\nFor extremely large forms, split UI into typed components or scoped form and\nfield groups instead of casting each field value.\n\n## Async defaults do not update\n\nThe Vue adapter observes reactive option objects. If data arrives after\n`useForm` runs, update `defaultValues` through a `reactive` options object or\nmount the editor only after the data exists. A plain object containing a\none-time snapshot is not reactive.\n\n## Composition types fail under Vue 3.5\n\nForm v2 requires Vue 3.6 or newer. The adapter's typed field components,\ninjection-based `AppForm`, and form composition rely on Vue 3.6 behavior that\nis not available in Vue 3.5.\n\n## Type instantiation is excessively deep\n\nThis TypeScript error usually involves a very large recursive value shape, a\nwidely inferred union, or unsupported composition. Reduce it to the smallest\nform that reproduces the problem, keep `defaultValues` concrete, and avoid\nunnecessary generic wrappers.\n\nIf the minimal reproduction still fails, report it in the\n[TanStack Form issue tracker](https://github.com/TanStack/form/issues). Include\nthe Vue and TypeScript versions, the form value type, and the smallest failing\nfield.\n\n## Errors exist but are not displayed\n\n`field.errors` respects the form's `errorVisibility` policy. Inspect\n`field.meta.original.errors` when debugging whether validation ran but the\nissues are intentionally hidden. Also confirm that the input calls\n`field.handleBlur` if the policy depends on `isBlurred`.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: debugging\ntitle: Debugging Vue Usage\n---\n\nThis page covers common Vue and TypeScript problems when using TanStack Form.\n\n## An input initially renders `undefined`\n\nEvery value rendered by an input must exist in form-level `defaultValues` from\nthe first render.\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { useForm } from '@tanstack/vue-form'\n\nconst form = useForm({\n  defaultValues: {\n    firstName: '',\n    subscribed: false,\n  },\n})\n</script>\n```\n\nDo not omit `defaultValues` or rely on a field-level default. When values come\nfrom an API, render a loading state before mounting the editable form or supply\na complete fallback shape.\n\n## A field value is `unknown`\n\nField names and values are inferred from `defaultValues`. Check that you have\nnot widened the initial object to `Record<string, unknown>`, `any`, or an\nunrelated union. Prefer a concrete value type:\n\n```ts\ntype Profile = { firstName: string; age: number }\n\nconst defaults: Profile = { firstName: '', age: 0 }\nconst form = useForm({ defaultValues: defaults })\n```\n\nFor extremely large forms, split UI into typed components or scoped form and\nfield groups instead of casting each field value.\n\n## Async defaults do not update\n\nThe Vue adapter observes reactive option objects. If data arrives after\n`useForm` runs, update `defaultValues` through a `reactive` options object or\nmount the editor only after the data exists. A plain object containing a\none-time snapshot is not reactive.\n\n## Composition types fail under Vue 3.5\n\nForm v2 requires Vue 3.6 or newer. The adapter's typed field components,\ninjection-based `AppForm`, and form composition rely on Vue 3.6 behavior that\nis not available in Vue 3.5.\n\n## Type instantiation is excessively deep\n\nThis TypeScript error usually involves a very large recursive value shape, a\nwidely inferred union, or unsupported composition. Reduce it to the smallest\nform that reproduces the problem, keep `defaultValues` concrete, and avoid\nunnecessary generic wrappers.\n\nIf the minimal reproduction still fails, report it in the\n[TanStack Form issue tracker](https://github.com/TanStack/form/issues). Include\nthe Vue and TypeScript versions, the form value type, and the smallest failing\nfield.\n\n## Errors exist but are not displayed\n\n`field.errors` respects the form's `errorVisibility` policy. Inspect\n`field.meta.original.errors` when debugging whether validation ran but the\nissues are intentionally hidden. Also confirm that the input calls\n`field.handleBlur` if the policy depends on `isBlurred`.\n"}
